# GymOS boundaries

- Feature UI lives in `packages/app` using Tamagui / RN primitives. No raw `<div>`, no raw `fetch`, no `Platform.OS`.
- Domain writes go through `packages/modules` public `index.ts` exports. Apps may compose; they must not invent a second auth or tenancy model.
- `packages/core` is pure TypeScript: nutrition math, money (bigint minor units), units, `can(actor, action, resource)`.
- Never fork per customer. Config or data, never `if (tenant === ...)`.
- Persistence paths use Luxon, not `new Date()`.
- ESLint `eslint-plugin-boundaries` is the mechanical enforcer. Do not weaken it to land a change.
